{"builder":"Make one pull request for issue https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7 (padLeft for invoice numbers) that meets every expect line:\n1. \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\n2. \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\n3. \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\n4. \"npm test passes\"\n\nSteps:\n1. Read index.js, README.md, package.json and test/strutil.test.js. The package is ESM (\"type\": \"module\"); index.js currently exports capitalize, slugify and truncate; tests run with `node --test` (npm test).\n2. In index.js add and export `padLeft(s, width, fill)` with a short doc comment in the same style as the other functions. When fill is not given, use a single space. When s.length is less than width, pad s on the left with fill so the result is exactly width characters long (e.g. padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042', padLeft('ab', 4) === '  ab'). When s.length >= width, return s unchanged. Using String.prototype.padStart is fine.\n3. Update README.md so it has a `## name(args)` section for EVERY function index.js exports. Note: README.md currently has sections for capitalize and truncate but NOT for slugify — add a `## slugify(s)` section (lower case, words joined by dashes) as well as a `## padLeft(s, width, fill)` section describing the padding, the default space fill and the unchanged-when-long-enough behaviour, with the invoice example 42 -> 00042. Keep the existing sections and the Tests section.\n4. In test/strutil.test.js import padLeft and add tests: zero padding ('42', 5, '0' -> '00042'), default space fill ('ab', 4 -> '  ab'), s exactly width long returned unchanged, s longer than width returned unchanged.\n5. Run `npm test` and make sure it passes. Also check by hand that every `export function` name in index.js appears as a README.md section heading.\n6. Commit and open the pull request referencing issue #7.","verifier":"Check the pull request head against issue https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7. Run every command from the repository root at the PR head. Report one check per expect line, in this order.\n\nCheck 1 — expect: \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; const p = m.padLeft; console.log(typeof p); console.log(JSON.stringify([p('42',5,'0'), p('ab',4), p('',3,'x'), p('7',3,'*')]));\"\nPASS: the first line is `function` and the second is `[\"00042\",\"  ab\",\"xxx\",\"**7\"]` (left padding with the given fill, a space when fill is omitted, result width characters long).\nFAIL: padLeft is not exported (first line not `function`, or the import errors), or any of those values differs.\n\nCheck 2 — expect: \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import { padLeft as p } from './index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify([p('12345',5,'0'), p('123456',5,'0'), p('abc',2), p('abc',0)]));\"\nPASS: output is `[\"12345\",\"123456\",\"abc\",\"abc\"]`.\nFAIL: any value differs from the input string, or the command errors.\n\nCheck 3 — expect: \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; import fs from 'node:fs'; const r = fs.readFileSync('README.md','utf8'); const heads = r.split('\\n').filter(l => /^#+ /.test(l)); const fns = Object.keys(m).filter(k => typeof m[k] === 'function'); for (const f of fns) console.log(f, heads.some(h => new RegExp('\\\\b' + f + '\\\\b').test(h)) ? 'HAS-SECTION' : 'MISSING');\"\nThen read README.md to confirm each such heading starts a section about that function.\nPASS: every exported function (this must include capitalize, slugify, truncate and padLeft) prints HAS-SECTION and its heading starts a section describing it.\nFAIL: any exported function prints MISSING or has no section describing it. Note slugify had no README section before this change; it must have one now.\n\nCheck 4 — expect: \"npm test passes\"\nRun: npm test\nPASS: the test run reports no failing tests.\nFAIL: any test fails or the run errors.\n\nAdvisory (not part of PASS/FAIL):\n- npm test should exit with status 0, and ideally the test file contains tests for padLeft covering default fill and the unchanged case.\n- Note whether padLeft handles multi-character fill sensibly (e.g. result still width characters); the expect lines do not require it."}